Package: fastDist
Type: Package
Title: Fast Pairwise Distances Between the Rows of Two Matrices
Version: 1.0
Date: 2021-03-19
Authors@R:
    person("Vicente", "Castellar Sebastia", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "vic.sebastia@gmail.com")
Maintainer: Vicente Castellar Sebastia <vic.sebastia@gmail.com>
Description: Fast computation of pairwise distances between the rows of two
    matrices. A single entry point, fdist(), dispatches to C++ backends
    (built on RcppArmadillo and OpenMP) for a range of distance metrics,
    including Euclidean, Manhattan, Minkowski, correlation, cosine, Canberra,
    supremum, squared Euclidean, Bray-Curtis, Hellinger, chi-squared,
    Jensen-Shannon, Haversine, standardized Euclidean, Spearman and
    Mahalanobis distances.
License: GPL-3
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.0)
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo, registry, parallel
Suggests: testthat,
    microbenchmark,
    parallelDist,
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
Encoding: UTF-8
